const a = await tools.progress.append_progress({content: `STAGE 3 - final answer (complete, stands on its own)
RANK: BFRQ-KARCHER-MASS | position=1 | reason=E12/E13 put the curved operation only in the code-vector estimator (Poincare Karcher step) while assignment, encoder, decoder, loss and Stage 3 stay untouched, which is the one footprint matching the frozen arm ordering in E6 where the Euclidean-assignment/prefix arms (l1_br_euclid 0.06207, l1_only 0.06233, resample 0.06363) beat every geometry-flavoured arm (successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500, v2 0.05463, tangent_successor_residual 0.05500), and every constant is derived from data (tau = median||z||, c = 1 unit, eta_k = 1/(1+N_k), 99th-pct clip, weights 1+log1p(mu_tilde) from E5/E10 transition mass).
RANK: poincare-frechet-successor-codebook | position=2 | reason=same estimator-level coupling but E12/E13 also move the assignment to Poincare distance and weight the commitment term, re-introducing the assignment-side curvature surface that lost in E6; its (indeg+1)/(n_v+2) clip[0.25,4] batch-normalised weights do guarantee a 16x spread so it will fire, unlike BFRQ's mild log1p weights, but eta=1 jumps at ~4 points per code cell (E10 mean out-degree 5.45) and eta=1/1/(1+N_k) damping is absent.
RANK: MIXCURV-FIBRE-RQ | position=3 | reason=the gating statistic (directed local clustering coefficient C_i) is never measured in the bundle - E10 reports only edge counts and out-degree, nothing on cycles among successors - and g_i defaults to 0.5 whenever k_i<5 while E5 shows the two lowest successor-count quintiles average 2.72 and 4.54 distinct successors, so roughly 40% of items stay inert; it also adds an unvalidated spherical fibre and two trainable curvatures back into the assignment metric, though its constants are at least documented defaults rather than tuned.
RANK: SUCC-GEO-CBTAB | position=4 | reason=its specified CHANGE/SPEC give a softplus triplet margin with no margin value and no coefficient against the RQ-VAE loss, i.e. free tunable constants in violation of the no-tuning policy, and its declared observables (level-1/level-2 successor prefix hit rate) target a dimension already saturated in E6/E7 (l1_br gold prefix alive 1.000/1.000/1.000/0.068 with recall 0.04671, the loss being at depth 4), while forcing level-L successor pairs together collides a near-unique SID space (E11 same_first_prefix_rate 0.0907 vs permuted null 0.067), the same family that scored 0.0550 in E6.`});
return a;

